# x86 ast-typed shim — Post-Fix Audit

File: openOODA/audit/x86-ast-typed-shim-post-fix.oot
Status: smoke — read-only static audit, no compilation run
Scope: ooda/oodac/x86_ast_typed.oo (Tier 5 #24 Turn 1) plus ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo caller, 2026-08-26
Baseline: audit/x86-ast-typed-shim.oot (98 lines, 5 risks filed)

---

## 1. Per-risk verification

Each row checks one of the 5 risks from the baseline audit.

| # | Risk | Severity | Fixed Y/N | Evidence (file:line) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Silent fallback to the 22-arm chain on Err | HIGH | Y | Ok arm returns at x86_emit.oo:89; Err arm calls process_exit(1) at x86_emit.oo:90; no fall-through past line 91 |
| 2 | Error tag leak from the chain (3 of 5 errors still carry `x86_ssa_compile:*` prefix) | MEDIUM | N | x86_ast_typed.oo:27 still does `return r;` verbatim; no re-tag, no wrap, no log; baseline §3 leak unchanged |
| 3 | Misleading "typed" naming (function name and Academy header promise type checking that does not exist) | MEDIUM | N | x86_ast_typed.oo:1 header still reads "Typed-AST dispatch shim"; x86_ast_typed.oo:17 function still named `x86_emit_stream_typed`; no rename, no header edit |
| 4 | Redundant `tokenize_lines` call (shim + chain both tokenize) | LOW | N | x86_ast_typed.oo:21 still calls `tokenize_lines(src)`; x86_ast_typed.oo:22 still guards `list_len(toks) == 0`; chain's own tokenize on x86_ssa_compile.oo:83 is unchanged |
| 5 | No newline normalization before runtime append (cosmetic double newline) | LOW | N | x86_ast_typed.oo:30 still reads `return Ok(asm_code + "\n" + x86_runtime_text());`; the leading `"\n"` is unchanged |

**Summary:** 1 of 5 risks fixed. 4 remain open.

